Subject: [PATCH 014/181] GL thread teardown handshake: stop before machine
 destruction

Exit-time msvcrt!memcpy AVs logged at roughly every second close. A
headless run (GL thread never spawned) still crashed at exit, exonerating
this thread - but harden it anyway: video_start registers a
MACHINE_NOTIFY_EXIT notifier (mvgl_exit) that flags the GL loop down and
waits up to 1 s for acknowledgement (RAII guard covers early-exit paths).
GL log now shows "machine exit" on every clean close. Residual post-exit
AV is the FFB plugin's teardown (TerminateProcess hook + scanner threads);
WER LocalDumps collect minidumps for attribution.

