The game renders a full 16:9 field of view already; the black margins were
ours. The mzgl canvas holds both page-flip buffers, and the 16:9 margin
clear riding the game's frame-sized fast-clear used a full-height scissor,
wiping the DISPLAYED page's margins at the start of every frame. Scope the
clear to the cleared page's rows (row0=addr/CW, nrows=count/CW), matching
add_span. Margins go 0% -> 75-100% lit in all 3D scenes; 2D stays 4:3.

Also adds the diagnostics that found it (all env-gated, inert when unset):
- MIDZ_PCLOG=<file> (zeus2.cpp): histogram of game-CPU PCs submitting
  FIFO draw commands (found the IRQ ring-drain at 0x0B686).
- MIDZ_RINGTAP=<file> (midzeus.cpp): RAM write tap for 0x24xxxxxx model
  headers (mapped the ring-fill library + HUD list builder).
- MIDZ_PATCH=<file> (midzeus.cpp): in-memory word patcher applied to the
  RAM program copy at machine_reset (ROM files untouched); built for the
