MIDV_FFB_SPRING creates an SDL_HAPTIC_SPRING condition effect alongside the
constant force, the way the plugin does for these games - its stock
FFBPlugin.ini carries EnableForceSpringEffectCrusnUSA=1 and this code only ever
created damper and friction.

A spring is POSITION-based, so its authority is greatest exactly where the
game's own motor force is smallest: around straight-ahead. Its absence is a
much more direct explanation of 'the self-centring near the centre feels
looser than normal' than anything in the conditioning chain, and it is a
missing feature rather than a regression - which also fits not being able to
say what normal was.

Off by default. The arcade cabinet's own mechanism is what it stands in for,
so the right amount depends on the base.

